From: Captain-Tripps
Subject: [PATCH] sycl prefill: EP reduce: keep card 1's rows buffer private (no exchange region)

With STRATA_EP_PREFILL_REDUCE=1 card 1 sums its own expert rows and card 0
reads only the sums (sum_reg); rows_reg.remote is read only when reduce is
off. rows_reg is then card 1's private buffer (its gathered inputs under the
gather alias, and its experts' outputs), but it was allocated as a shared
exchange region.

On Linux that region is card 1 VRAM plus an IPC mapping, so the only change
there is one IPC handle fewer. Where the region has to be host USM (a port
without Level Zero IPC, e.g. Windows), every expert GEMM on card 1 read and
wrote it over PCIe, at a speed set by the pinned pages a process got.

Add ep_region_alloc_private (zeMemAllocDevice on the owner, no remote
mapping; freed by ep_region_free) and use it for rows_reg when reduce is
on. If it does not fit, fall back to the shared region with a log line.
STRATA_EP_PREFILL_ROWS_HOST=1 restores the old allocation.

Measured (Windows, 2x Arc Pro B70, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_S, 37,318-token
prompt, 4 fresh starts per arm, same binary):
  private:     1557 1561 1476 1570 tok/s prompt read (first token ~24 s)
  shared host:  777  775  780  774 tok/s              (first token ~48 s)
Decode unchanged; greedy output identical to the previous build on 5 fixed
prompts including a ~37k-token one. Card 1 free VRAM after setup: 2,060 ->
1,264 MiB (the 800 MiB buffer moves into VRAM).
Linux / IPC path: not measured; expected neutral.

---
diff --git a/sycl/src/prefill/prefill.cpp b/sycl/src/prefill/prefill.cpp
index 3d046dc..ce67e99 100644
--- a/sycl/src/prefill/prefill.cpp
+++ b/sycl/src/prefill/prefill.cpp
@@ -2032,8 +2032,24 @@ bool Prefill::set_ep_peer(int device, core::ExpertCache* cache, std::string& err
     pp->reduce_rows = reduce && reduce[0] == '1';
     const char* push = std::getenv("STRATA_EP_PREFILL_PUSH");
     pp->reduce_push = pp->reduce_rows && push && push[0] == '1';
-    bool ok = core::ep_region_alloc(device, primary, (size_t) m.T_max * N * 2, pp->x_reg, err) &&
-              core::ep_region_alloc(device, primary, (size_t) m.T_max * K * N * 4, pp->rows_reg, err);
+    // With STRATA_EP_PREFILL_REDUCE card 1 sums its own rows and card 0 reads only the sums (sum_reg): rows_reg is then
+    // card 1's private buffer (its gathered inputs under the gather alias, and its experts' outputs). Keep it in card 1's
+    // VRAM without an IPC mapping: where ep_region_alloc has to give host memory (a port without Level Zero IPC, e.g.
+    // Windows) every expert GEMM read and wrote it over PCIe.
+    // STRATA_EP_PREFILL_ROWS_HOST=1 restores the shared region.
+    static const bool rows_host = [] { const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_EP_PREFILL_ROWS_HOST"); return v && v[0] == '1'; }();
+    bool rows_private = pp->reduce_rows && !rows_host;
+    bool ok = core::ep_region_alloc(device, primary, (size_t) m.T_max * N * 2, pp->x_reg, err);
+    if (ok && rows_private && !core::ep_region_alloc_private(device, (size_t) m.T_max * K * N * 4, pp->rows_reg, err)) {
+        std::fprintf(stderr, "strata prefill: card 1's rows buffer does not fit in its VRAM (%s): shared region instead\n",
+                     err.c_str());
+        err.clear();
+        rows_private = false;
+    }
+    if (ok && !rows_private) ok = core::ep_region_alloc(device, primary, (size_t) m.T_max * K * N * 4, pp->rows_reg, err);
+    if (ok) std::fprintf(stderr, "strata prefill: expert parallel: card 1's rows buffer (%zu MiB) in %s%s\n",
+                         ((size_t) m.T_max * K * N * 4) >> 20, rows_private ? "its VRAM" : "the shared exchange region",
+                         rows_private ? "" : " (STRATA_EP_PREFILL_ROWS_HOST=1 or no reduce)");
     if (ok) pp->rows_bytes = (size_t) m.T_max * K * N * 4;
     if (ok && pp->reduce_rows)
         ok = core::ep_region_alloc(pp->reduce_push ? primary : device, pp->reduce_push ? device : primary,
diff --git a/sycl/include/strata/core/ep_mem.hpp b/sycl/include/strata/core/ep_mem.hpp
index affcd73..024f23a 100644
--- a/sycl/include/strata/core/ep_mem.hpp
+++ b/sycl/include/strata/core/ep_mem.hpp
@@ -53,6 +53,24 @@ inline bool ep_region_alloc(int owner, int other, size_t bytes, EpRegion& r, std
     return true;
 }
 
+/// `bytes` zeroed on dpct device `owner`, for the owner's own kernels only (remote stays null): a buffer that sits in the
+/// exchange machinery but is never read by the other card, so it needs no IPC handle (and, on a port where
+/// ep_region_alloc must fall back to host memory, stays in VRAM). Freed by ep_region_free like any region.
+inline bool ep_region_alloc_private(int owner, size_t bytes, EpRegion& r, std::string& err) {
+    r = EpRegion{};
+    r.owner_ctx = ep_ze_context(owner);
+    ze_device_mem_alloc_desc_t desc{};
+    desc.stype = ZE_STRUCTURE_TYPE_DEVICE_MEM_ALLOC_DESC;
+    ze_result_t z = zeMemAllocDevice(r.owner_ctx, &desc, bytes, 4096, ep_ze_device(owner), &r.local);
+    if (z != ZE_RESULT_SUCCESS) {
+        err = "expert parallel: zeMemAllocDevice of " + std::to_string(bytes) + " bytes failed (" + std::to_string((unsigned) z) + ")";
+        r.local = nullptr;
+        return false;
+    }
+    dpct::dev_mgr::instance().get_device(owner).in_order_queue().memset(r.local, 0, bytes).wait();
+    return true;
+}
+
 inline void ep_region_free(EpRegion& r) {
     if (r.remote != nullptr) zeMemCloseIpcHandle(r.other_ctx, r.remote);
     if (r.local != nullptr) zeMemFree(r.owner_ctx, r.local);
